# New-interface loading

For views rendered under `/new`, follow `docs/NEW_LOOK_LOADING.md` and the repository `AGENTS.md`.

Use `PageSkeleton` for full-view loading, and the primitives in `skeleton-sections.tsx` for independent regions. Match the actual page structure; do not substitute a generic spinner or “Loading…” card. Cover route/Suspense, initial data, and access/feature checks.

Only show a skeleton when the current user/budget/filter scope has no usable data. Background refresh preserves existing content and drafts. Errors, empty results, and user-initiated actions have their own states.
